{"id": "youtube:UgwoDT6tVpx75aQJ79F4AaABAg.AQcnnKk5fGXAQd89cNbZHg", "text": "· Self-published (Kepler interactive are actually 7 indie devs companies)\r\n· Sandfall has said Clair Obscur cost around 10 millions to make, way less than an average AA game\r\n· 33 people is considered small, despite of hire companies to assist in some things like animation (credits are longer than 33 people, but in Silksong you can see around 100 people in credits)\r\n\r\nActually I dont know where the line between AA and indie must be, I just highlights what I think makes this game an indie game!", "language": "en", "event_tag": "tga_2025_sweep", "label_llm": "pos", "llm_confidence": "med", "source": "youtube"}
{"id": "youtube:UgwpBy8NeTtzPmj4vnJ4AaABAg.ARFBdluoEXhARFWtKs_dRX", "text": "​@MrMorvanaA game explicitly being stripped of its title of GotY for using is a lot different than a game made by AI won GoTY. \n\nE33's AI use was already publicly known.  This didn't make anyone aware that it used AI.  \n\nThis is now a matter of \"this game using AI is GotY\" vs \"this game does not deserve GoTY because it used AI.\"\nThose are the only options, and the former is significantly more harmful.  \n\nY'all need to stop defending the AI game and saying it should have kept its title.  It is not more harmful to strip it of its title.  It doesn't deserve it.", "language": "en", "event_tag": "indie_game_awards_rescinded", "label_llm": "neg", "llm_confidence": "high", "source": "youtube"}
{"id": "youtube:UgwpN3auNglO7vtiXSB4AaABAg", "text": "To some extent I understand. However, now that this has been done let it be a precedent.\n\nI also agree at the non thriller of Ai being part of society. This is primarily because we can see it's mi's use vastly out saying positive use.", "language": "en", "event_tag": "indie_game_awards_rescinded", "label_llm": "neu", "llm_confidence": "med", "source": "youtube"}
